    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="48.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 48.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/> afylle, beo he utlah, ⁊ his hente mid hearme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.star"/> ælc þæra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2-3"/> þe riht wylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.3"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he man afylle, beo he utlage, ⁊ his hænte mid hearme ælc ðara ðe riht wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he man afylle, beo he utlah, ⁊ his hente mid hearme ælc þara þe riht wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>Si aliquem occidat, sit útlaga, et capiat eum cum clamore (damno<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1-2"/>) omnis qui rectum diligit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (uelit).</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si hominem occiderit, sit exul et cum clamore expellatur ab omnibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1-4"/> qui Dei iusticiam uolunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2-4"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="347" ed="#liebermann"/>[48, 2] Si autem hominem occidat, sit exlex, et eum prosequa[tu]r [cum] -dampno quicumque amator iusticie est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="48.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="200" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf he man afylle, beo he utlage ⁊ his hænte mid hearme ælc ðara ðe riht wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="280" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif he mann afylle, beo he utlah and his hente mid hearme ælc þæra þe riht wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="346" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.de.1"/> er einen Menschen [dabei] erschlägt, sei er friedlos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.de.2"/>, und fahnde auf ihn mit Gerüfte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_48-2.lnote.de.3"/> jeder derer, die Gesetzlichkeit wünschen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If he kills a man [in doing so], let him be an outlaw, and let everyone who desires right pursue him with the hue and cry.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_48-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="201" ed="#robertson"/>If he kills a man, he shall be outlawed, and he shall be pursued with hostility<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_48-2.robnote.n.2"/> by all those who wish to promote law and order.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="469" ed="#whitelock"/>If he slays a man, he is to be an outlaw, and each of those who wish to uphold the law are to pursue him with hostility.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="281" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If he kills someone, he shall be outlawed and hunted without regard for his safety by those who desire to uphold the law.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="346"><ref target="clause:EGu_6-6">EGu 6.6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. E Gu. 6, 6</note>
        <note type="editorial">‘hearme’ (harm) is the archetype's reading for ‘hreame’ (hue and cry), as in EGu 6.6. Liebermann compares EGu 6.6.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 347, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prosequar <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prosequar Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Dm;</hi> cla. <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi> 11,11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above Dm; cla. Hn 11,11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> u. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d. K; u. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">man <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">man Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so für</hi> hreame <hi rend="italic">Archetyp mit E Gu.</hi> 6, 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus the archetype, for hreame, in agreement with E Gu. 6, 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðara <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðara Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">346</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wille <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wille Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hominibus <hi rend="italic">Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hominibus Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">347</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uoluerint <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uoluerint Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 11, 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 11, 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">In <hi rend="italic">misericordia regis</hi> verfällt diese Missetat nach Hn 13, 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">According to Hn 13, 11 this misdeed falls <hi rend="italic">in misericordia regis</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_48-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">209</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sinnwidrig sehen in <hi rend="italic">hearme</hi> die gewöhnliche Bed. <hi rend="italic">damno</hi> Q i C; aus Zusammenhang erraten richtig <hi rend="italic">clamore</hi> (<hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 29³) Q ii Inst.—Irriges <hi rend="italic">expellatur</hi> in Inst, das ich hätte <hi rend="spaced">sperren</hi> sollen, verführte Kolderup zum Vergleiche der Saxo-Stelle <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. S. 91 zu EGu 6, 6³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q i C, contrary to the sense, see in <hi rend="italic">hearme</hi> the usual meaning <hi rend="italic">damno</hi>; Q ii Inst correctly guess <hi rend="italic">clamore</hi> (<hi rend="italic">above</hi> 29³) from the context.—The erroneous <hi rend="italic">expellatur</hi> in Inst, which I ought to have <hi rend="italic">spaced</hi>, misled Kolderup into comparing the passage of Saxo <hi rend="italic">above</hi> p. 91 on EGu 6, 6³</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_48-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. E. and G. 6, 6 and note.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_48-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Schmid, followed by Liebermann, regards <hi rend="italic">hearme</hi> as a metathesised form of <hi rend="italic">hreame</hi> (cf. <hi rend="italic">cum clamore</hi>, Q, Inst.), but see the note to E. and G., <hi rend="italic">loc. cit.</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
